{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KKxYMFXfY2dhkjynCtPkyi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, single-target works correctly in the success case. Now let me compile all the differences I've found:\n\n1. **Error message capitalization** — syscall errors are lowercase on macOS (`file exists`, `no such file or directory`) but GNU uses capitalized versions (`File exists`, `No such file or directory`). Need a `sysErrMsg` function like mkdir has.\n\n2. **R1.3 directory error format** — ours wraps target in quotes `'testdir': hard link not allowed for directory`, gln doesn't: `testdir: hard link not allowed for directory`.\n\n3. **Multi-target, last not a directory** — our message is `target 'X' is not a directory`, gln distinguishes:\n   - Last doesn't exist: `target 'X': No such file or directory`\n   - Last exists but not dir: `target 'X': Not a directory`\n\n4. **Single-target link name** — when single target, gln uses `./basename` as the link name (visible in error messages). Our code uses just `basename`. Functionally equivalent for success, but error messages differ.\n\n5. **Missing `Implements` comment** — the file needs the package doc comment referencing the implemented requirements.\n\nNow I'm going to fix these issues systematically, starting with adding the package documentation comment that references the requirements.\n\nWriting corrected file...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":36473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fc66413-5509-443d-b291-04e23843da1d","uuid":"05764580-b439-4be1-bbea-58147921c3f3"}
